Key design decisions:
- Properties() generated for ALL types (not just those with own runtime props) so
  that abstract root types with no parent return nil instead of missing from method set.
- boolToUint64 in core.go to avoid re-declaration across generated files.
- PropKey<N> = N constants (not name-based): 107 property names appear with multiple
  key.int values, making name-based constants ambiguous.
- passthrough:true excluded from Properties() (computed, not serialized).
- runtime:false excluded entirely from struct + Properties().
- callback type skipped (no serializable state).
- 'double' type: float64 in struct, PropertyTypeFloat (wire as float32 per binary spec).
- Id type: uint64 via typeRuntime override (all runtime Id props have typeRuntime='uint').
- List<Id>: []byte (encoded blob, same as Bytes).

