task: T-364
commit: d1b0b95
date: 2026-05-08
status: COMPLETE

## Root cause
`anim.go` emit() had: `if a.speed != 1.0 { la.Speed = a.speed }`.
When speed is the default (1.0), la.Speed stayed at Go zero (0.0).
Serializer condition `if o.Speed != 1` then saw 0.0 != 1 → true → encoded Speed=0.0.
Rive WASM runtime read Speed=0 and froze all animations.

## Fix
Removed guard. Now: `la.Speed = a.speed` always.
Default animConfig.speed=1.0, so serializer correctly skips encoding.

## Verification
- All unit tests pass (GOTMPDIR=/app/workspace/tmp go test ./...)
- Examples regenerated: 3 animation .rivs dropped the erroneous Speed=0 property
- rivtool inspect confirms Speed absent from encoded props (runtime uses default 1.0)
- Fps and Duration defaults (60, 60) already correct — no change needed

## Coverage from defaults-map.json
All other non-zero defaults are handled:
- Shape/Rect/Ellipse/Node: Opacity, ScaleX/Y, OriginX/Y (0.5), BlendModeValue — builder/shape.go ✓
- Fill/Stroke: IsVisible, BlendModeValue — builder/shape.go ✓
- Stroke.Thickness: serializer guard `if != 1` — gen_shapes.go ✓
- Rectangle.LinkCornerRadius: serializer guard `if !` — gen_shapes.go ✓
- Artboard: Opacity, ScaleX/Y, BlendModeValue, FractionalWidth/Height, sentinel IDs — builder/builder.go ✓
- Animation.Fps (60) and Duration (60): always assigned from animConfig defaults ✓
- Animation.Speed (1.0): THIS FIX ✓

