[T-368] PROJ_RIVE-GO_CODE_FIX_PARENTID_INDEXING — 2026-05-08

ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED:
  builder/shape.go stored global object indices as parentId, but the Rive
  runtime expects artboard-relative indices (artboard=0, child1=1, etc.).
  Example: Shape at global[2] with artboard at global[1] emitted parentId=1,
  which the runtime read as "parent = artboard-relative[1] = Shape itself" → loop.

FORMULA: artboard_relative = global_index − artboard_global_index

CHANGES (commit 619126a):
  - builder.go: pass artboardOffset to childEmitter interface; direct children
    receive parentIdx=0 (artboard is relative 0)
  - shape.go: all idx computations subtract artboardOffset; fixes parentId on
    shapes, paths, fills, paints, gradients
  - anim.go: CubicEaseInterpolator index made artboard-relative (InterpolatorId);
    KeyedObject.ObjectId fixed automatically (shapeIdx now artboard-relative)
  - builder_test.go: assertions updated to artboard-relative expectations
  - All docs/preview/examples/*.riv regenerated

VERIFICATION:
  - minimal_static.riv: Rectangle parentId=0501 ✓, Fill parentId=0501 ✓,
    SolidColor parentId=0503 ✓
  - fade_rect.riv: KeyedObject.ObjectId=1 (Shape at artboard-relative 1) ✓
  - All 19 builder tests + all rive round-trip tests pass

NOTE on parentId=0 (Artboard root):
  gen_root.go suppresses emission when ParentId==0. The Rive runtime treats
  missing parentId as default (artboard root), so suppressing 0 is correct
  and equivalent to emitting 05 00. Reference files explicitly emit 05 00
  but both forms are valid.

ALSO NOTEWORTHY — T-367 is a spec error (raised blocker):
  T-367 claims ToC packing uses 4x too many uint32s. Empirical decode of
  ball_test.riv proves the current 4-keys/uint32 algorithm is correct.
  The task's "fix" (16-keys/uint32) would produce files unreadable by our
  own reader.go. Awaiting Silas direction on T-367.

